---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---
<Marketing
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with Total Recall and theo: email support, setup guides, and what to include so we can fix things fast."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(32px,4.6vw,52px);margin:10px 0 0">Get help.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:18px 0 0">
        A real person reads every message. Email
        <a href="mailto:support@totalrecallhq.com">support@totalrecallhq.com</a> and we will get
        back to you within two business days, usually much sooner.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:40px;display:grid;gap:28px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65">
        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Help us help you</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Three things make almost every issue fixable on the first reply: the email address you
            sign in with, what you were doing when it went wrong (which setup step, or what you
            asked theo), and what you expected versus what actually happened. Screenshots are
            gold, including any error message word for word.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Guides and documentation</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Setup guides and reference documentation live at
            <a href="/docs">totalrecallhq.com/docs</a>. If you are mid-setup, the wizard itself is
            the best guide: each step names the exact screen you should be on and what to paste
            where.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Security issues</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Found something that looks like a security problem? Email
            <a href="mailto:support@totalrecallhq.com?subject=Security">support@totalrecallhq.com</a>
            with "Security" in the subject line and we will treat it as the front of the queue.
            Please do not post details publicly before we have had a chance to fix it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Your data, your accounts</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Your brain runs in your own Supabase and Railway accounts, so some fixes happen on
            infrastructure only you can log in to. We will never ask for your passwords or API
            keys in email; when support needs hands-on access, we use revocable member invites you
            approve and can remove at any time. More on how your data is handled is in the
            <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
